===META
Title: SOLUM Language Specification
Author: Pomilon
Version: 1.0.0
===

> SOLUM Specification (written in SOLUM)

SOLUM is a high-performance, unambiguous markup language designed for maximum predictability.

>> Block Elements

Block elements must start at the very beginning of a line. Crucially, most block markers must be followed by a space to be recognized.

>>> 1. Headers
. {> Header} $$ \rightarrow $$ Level 1
. {>> Header} $$ \rightarrow $$ Level 2
. {>>> Header} $$ \rightarrow $$ Level 3
. {># Header} $$ \rightarrow $$ Auto-numbered Header

>>> 2. Lists
. {. Item} $$ \rightarrow $$ Unordered
. {1. Item} $$ \rightarrow $$ Ordered
. {a. Item} $$ \rightarrow $$ Alpha
. Nesting: achieved by increasing dots (e.g., {.. Item} is Level 2)

>>> 3. Quotes
. Block: {[q]} content {[q]}
. Line-based: {` Quote} (Level 1), {`` Quote} (Level 2)

>>> 4. Tables
. Enclosed in {[t]} markers.
. Cells separated by {||}.
. Use {---} for header separation.

[t]
Marker || Type
---
> || Header
. || List
[t]

>>> 5. Specialized Blocks
. Code: {{cpp: ... }}
. Literal: === ... ===
. Math Block: $$$ ... $$$

>> Inline Elements

!!Bold!!, ::Italic::, ==Underline==, %%Highlight%%, ~~Strike~~, {Inline Code}, and ''Inline Literal''.

>>> Assets and Math
. Links: {[@ url "label"]}
. Images: {[! path "alt"]}
. Inline Math: $$E=mc^2$$
. Tasks: {[ ]} and {[x]}
. Escaping: {\!!} renders as !!

>> Logic Showcase

SOLUM handles overlapping styles gracefully:
!!Bold and ::Bold-Italic!! Italic::

$$$
\text{Performance} = O(n)
$$$
